spec: docs/typepedia.md, docs/di.md

why: `PartialFunction[Request, Response ! Async]` is the type this
  stack writes most and reads worst. The operator's choice, after the
  candidates were measured against THIS repository's precedence: the
  alias must bind looser than `!`, which rules out `~>`, `-?>` and
  `=?>` (all three misparse `A X B ! F` as `(A X B) ! F`), and `=?>`
  would sit one transposition away from `?=>` besides.

what: `infix type |=>[A, B] = PartialFunction[A, B]` in the core,
  beside the other infix types; used in the DI routes example and the
  guide; a line in the typepedia with the precedence reason. NOT a
  repo-wide sweep — other modules adopt it when they touch the code.

next: add it, use it where it is mine to use, document why
